{"ref":"BDB, מַשְׁחִית²","hw":"מַשְׁחִית²","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מַשְׁחִית</span></big>  <strong>n.</strong>[<strong>m.</strong>] <strong>ruin, destruction</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 5:26\" href=\"/Jeremiah.5.26\">Je 5:26</a> + 10 times;—physical <em>destruction</em> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 5:16\" href=\"/Ezekiel.5.16\">Ez 5:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 9:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.9.6\">9:6</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 21:36\" href=\"/Ezekiel.21.36\">21:36</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 25:15\" href=\"/Ezekiel.25.15\">25:15</a>; <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:13\" href=\"/Exodus.12.13\">Ex 12:13</a> (P), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 20:23\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.20.23\">2 Ch 20:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 22:4\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.22.4\">22:4</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּעַל מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 18:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.18.9\">Pr 18:9</a> = <em>destroyers;</em> <a data-ref=\"Daniel 10:8\" href=\"/Daniel.10.8\">Dn 10:8</a> (disfigurement); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:25\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.25\">Je 51:25</a> (fig. of Bab. as destroyer), in <a data-ref=\"II Kings 23:13\" href=\"/II_Kings.23.13\">2 K 23:13</a> = <em>mt. of corruption</em> (where <em>bamoth</em> were, S. end of Mt. of Olives, poss. adapted from <span dir=\"rtl\">הַר־מִשְׁחָה</span> so Hoffm<sup>ZAW ii (1882), 175</sup> Benz Kit Bur; 𝔙 <em>mons offensionis</em>).—v. [<a data-ref=\"BDB, שָׁחַת\" href=\"/BDB,_שָׁחַת\", dir=\"rtl\">שָׁחַת</a>] <strong>Hiph. 1.</strong> Pt.","next":"BDB, מַשְׁחֵת","prev":"BDB, שָׁחַת"}